    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρῦλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>noise as of many voices,
			murmur</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				286
			</span></i> (pl.,= <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				2.199
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.Lac.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1786.1
			</span></i> F., <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>—This word and its cognates are written with one
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ</span> in Papyri and best codd. (cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1307.42
			</span></i>), with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λλ</span> (as Batr.l.c.) in
			inferior codd., also in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLips.</u>
				40 ii 10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>.</div>
